## Local / Windows test identity (HARD)

Sacb0y’s installed Palace uses Identity **Name** `C20A7629-6BDE-449F-958A-5AAF8BCE88F3` (see `CatalogStore.ReleasePackageName` and committed `Package.appxmanifest`). Agents must **never** touch that install.

### Always

1. **Separate test identity.** Before any register/launch, use a **copied** `Package.appxmanifest` whose Identity **Name**, `PhoneProductId`, and `DisplayName` are **not** the release package (Name and PhoneProductId must not be `C20A7629-…`; DisplayName must not stay `Palace`). Prefer `.\scripts\Prepare-TestIdentity.ps1 -IdentityName <Name>` (rewrites all three). `.ps1` files stay ASCII-only so Windows PowerShell 5.1 can parse them.
2. **Launch guard.** `.\BuildAndRun.ps1` **refuses** Identity `C20A7629-…` and exits non-zero. Do not bypass the guard. Do not call `winapp run` / `Add-AppxPackage` yourself against the release manifest.
3. **`PALACE_DATA_DIR` + temp SFW.** Point data at an isolated temp folder. Use a temp safe-for-work media copy only.
4. After a test session, restore the **repo file** `Package.appxmanifest` from git / the Prepare backup so the release Name is not committed. That is **not** restoring Sacb0y’s install.
5. **Register the build manifest.** `winapp run --no-launch` copies the **source** `Package.appxmanifest` into the layout and registers that copy. The source manifest has **no** Windows App Runtime package dependency (the SDK writes `Microsoft.WindowsAppRuntime` only into the generated build manifest). The registered app then crashes with **REGDB_E_CLASSNOTREG**. Register the **build output’s own** `bin\...\AppxManifest.xml` instead — the file the Windows App SDK generated for that configuration — and only after its Identity **Name** is a separate test name. Do not register by `winapp run --no-launch`.

### Never

| Forbidden | Why |
|---|---|
| `winapp run` / `.\BuildAndRun.ps1` / `Add-AppxPackage` on release Identity `C20A7629-…` or an unpatched release `Package.appxmanifest` | Overwrites his packaged install |
| `winapp run … --no-launch` on release Identity | Still **registers layout** and can overwrite his install |
| `winapp run --no-launch` to register any identity (including a test name) | Copies the source `Package.appxmanifest` (no WindowsAppRuntime dependency) → **REGDB_E_CLASSNOTREG**. Register `bin\...\AppxManifest.xml` instead |
| `Add-AppxPackage` of a build `AppxManifest.xml` whose Identity Name is still `C20A7629-…` | Same overwrite as registering the release manifest |
| `winapp unregister` (or Remove-AppxPackage) on his `C20A7629-…` install | Destroys his install; **agents do not restore it — Sacb0y owns that** |
| Real catalog, Unity trees, `%TEMP%\palace-vss` | Not agent test data |

### Sacb0y owns C20A7629

If his install is broken or missing, **stop**. Do not re-register `C20A7629-…`. Report the blocker; Sacb0y installs/restores main himself.
